CORE libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[handler\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ terminate: non-throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[handler\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ plain: non-throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member throws: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ base throws: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ template: non-throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ noexcept\(false\): SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Destructors without a noexcept-specifier were taken as potentially
throwing, the noexcept operator took every destructor call as
non-throwing, and the noexcept of a destructor declared in its class was
not recorded at all (rConstructorDecl).  The handler runs on paths 1 and
4 (g++ and clang++ agree on each path).
